#Problem
Given an array of positive integers nums and a positive integer target, return the minimal length of a subarray whose sum is greater than or equal to target.
If there is no such subarray, return 0 instead.

Example 1:
Input:int target = 7;
int[] nums = new int[]{2, 3, 1, 2, 4, 3};
Output: 2

Example 2:
Input:int target = 4;
int[] nums = new int[]{1, 4, 4};
Output: 1


#Intuition
We should increase range of elements until sum of them will be equal or more then target.
When target is reached we should shrink array until sum of elements will be less than target. And always calculate and return minimum array.

#Approach


#Algorithm


#Complexity
-Time complexity
O(n)


-Space complexity
Auxiliary Space

Total Space


#Code
    static public int minSubArrayLen(int target, int[] nums) {
        int minArrayLentgh = 0;
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0, j = 0; j < nums.length; j++) {
            sum += nums[j];
            if (sum >= target) {
                while (sum - nums[i] >= target) {
                    sum -= nums[i];
                    i++;
                }
                int minSize = j - i + 1;
                minArrayLentgh = minArrayLentgh > 0 ? Math.min(minArrayLentgh, minSize) : minSize;
            }
        }
        return minArrayLentgh;
    }
